root=Path('/workspace/scratch/e6eabdc4c3a0/detective-v10')
rows = [
('INTRO07','Mimi wants an organized entrance; her children spot the missing phone.','Shared folder and exceptionally secure filing sound like office banter before we know the family. Three lines each contain more than one joke.','Lost-phone captain; Dilo claiming the fastest solve; Luli bringing a book.','Make the missing phone immediately visible and let the children answer it in their own short styles. Dilo can tease Mom without a lesson.'),
('CASEWALL12','Dilo wants the whole wall for theories; the others try to fit in.','Shelf, appointment, cushion, waiting fact and evidence-space lesson compete. Nini and Alio also sound like adult satirists; Mimi gives a moral after the invitation.','Theories hogging a real wall; Nini wanting a cushion; family negotiating limited space.','Keep one physical escalation that each person can picture. Let someone play along; end on a family consequence, not a reminder of evidence rules already printed above.'),
('CASE01','Alio wants his grand tunnel/minivan explanation to count.','No courier is already explicit in the intro. Nini repeats follow-the-facts instruction; Dilo explains the parking joke for three sentences. Alio alone supplies foolishness.','Tunnel/minivan; Luli’s pointed zero-evidence jab; Dilo’s blocked notes.','Use an absurdly overlarge theory in the margin, then a quick comeback. The intro supplies the investigation, so the banter need not teach it again.'),
('CASE02','Alio suspects the Cup’s manner; the real worry is a blank return record.','Luli explains lawful sign-out and polishing before the paperwork turn; Mimi’s Better sounds like grading a child. Promotion adds a corporate metaphor.','Suspiciously good posture / its paperwork; Nini keeping watch over the well-behaved Cup.','Let Alio make the useful paperwork observation himself. Short straight reply, pivot, family tag; retain the Cup’s dignity without four explanations.'),
('CASE03','Nini promotes a sparkle; Dilo worries it will replace him.','Reflection, recovery from not being in charge, practiced shelf-standing and whole-room instruction elongate one simple appointment joke.','Inspector Glitter; Mostly sparkling; Dilo competing with a sparkle; shedding glitter reply.','Let Nini enjoy her named object and allow Luli’s answer to be a joke rather than a disciplinary correction. Keep the photo task clear from its context.'),
('CASE04','Dilo and Alio want the box to behave like an evasive witness.','Two people separately explain that boxes cannot answer. Mimi’s seal update and Nini’s someone-we-can-ask make the adults/youngest correctors.','Suspicion with paperwork; professional staring; Mimi promising the helmet if it blinks.','Trust children to know a box cannot talk. One practical bridge to Pixel is enough; keep the staring contest and adult participation.'),
('CASE05','Dilo is staking his reputation on the locker contest.','The door question is said twice, and every line adds a second comic explanation. Conflict of interest is harder at the young end, though the refusal itself is clear.','It has been briefed; badge question; Dilo treating a door as a rival.','Keep the competitive game with concise replies. Let the badge refusal have an immediate concrete stake if needed; do not define the phrase or add a moral.'),
('THREAD34','Dilo wants an easy printer answer; Nini wants names she can use.','Dear Dilo restates straightforward; Luli explains his whole personality; Nini’s list ends by explaining why it is unhelpful. Four voices share the same explanatory cadence.','Luli knowing he would complain either way; Nini tired of the thing; Bibi checking printer’s references.','Treat it as tired family chatter around a strange printer. Use the marks and incomplete route as mystery tension, then leave the references joke unglossed.'),
('CASE06','Nini wants the promised dragon; Luli shares her disappointment.','Emotionally prepared, qualifications and history-book chapter layer adult abstractions onto a wonderfully obvious spoon disappointment. The final line explains keeping fantasy out of evidence.','Perhaps the dragon was a cook; soup; Bibi putting history on shelves; pencil dragon in margin.','Let the imaginary dragon grow through play, with Luli joining it. One necessary label question suffices; Bibi can object affectionately without dismissing Nini’s drawing.'),
('CASE07','Alio wants his dramatic cupboard search to have been useful; Mimi is tired of cupboards.','Opening slowly is explained twice, Nini describes where all coats would go, and the closing task reminder interrupts the broom joke.','Only dramatic cupboards; eliminating tiny cupboards; Mimi talking to brooms.','Maintain a clear moon-costume size joke, give Alio a defensible practical result, and let Mimi be tired and funny herself.'),
('CASE08','Alio wants a beautifully straight shortcut; buildings refuse it.','Appointment metaphor drags; Mimi’s use-doors line treats Alio like a fool who has never entered a building. Load-bearing is a possible unfamiliar term.','Have you shown it to the walls; building rejecting draft; Dilo holding map rather than roof.','Make obstacle/map mismatch concrete. Alio’s reply should show he understands his mistake and can answer back; one physical roof/wall punch is enough.'),
('CASE09','Bibi recognizes something but wants it checked; Alio wants promised cake.','Bibi explains memory discipline already stated in the intro; cake receives an extra announcement and bakery investigation after reliable source/terrible delivery has landed.','Bibi’s limited memory; self-promised cake; reliable source, terrible delivery; children helping Bibi check.','Keep Bibi allowed to be uncertain without a speech. Cake should reveal Alio’s appetite and self-importance, then stop at its best turn.'),
('CASE10','Dilo likes the rover and its cable but needs the access record.','Nobody move/I can complicate this labels him incompetent. Luli grades him twice; Dilo requests credit for being sensible. A robot expert becomes a child supervised by a teacher.','Two owners/one rover; cable as possible third owner; Luli volunteering to untangle it.','Give Dilo ownership of a useful decision without a reward speech. Sibling mockery can target the cable or dismantling urge, with Dilo able to return it.'),
('CASE11','Children catch organized Mimi hiding phone beside breakfast; she defends herself.','Undercover and source jokes are followed by explanations of compartments and the profession, weakening the fast call-and-response.','Whole source six-turn chain, especially Does the oat bar know / We protect our sources / You would not.','This is model family teasing: children land the charge and Mom answers rather than preaching. Keep its bite; remove the explanations after the evasions.'),
('CASE12','Dilo wants a serious parrot interview; parrot wants a cracker; Nini understands the negotiation.','Try listening before your next question sounds superior. Statement consistency, lunch order, handler and Alio biscuits offer too many alternative endings.','Please speak clearly for the notebook; snack price; first interview with snack budget.','Let Nini translate the bird’s priority rather than instruct Dilo how to listen. One strong snack-budget payoff; handler remains real, not a new invented clue.'),
('CASE13','Alio wants to rescue his fox-camera theory from its obvious equipment problem.','V9 gives Luli two dismissals and Nini two more practical objections, then makes Alio retire with dignity: a pile-on. Source Nini joined his fantasy with a strap.','Pockets; tiny camera strap; Alio welcoming someone taking equipment seriously.','Restore a playmate for Alio. His answer should sharpen the joke, not surrender to correction. The real photo can re-enter naturally without unfoxy evidence lecture.'),
('CASE14','Luli recalls feeding her bag books instead of feeding herself; the family remembers.','Opening threatens to arrest a clock; lunch recollection then repeats who shared lunch, book contribution, recipes and a distant cake callback. Long scene wanders from memory mix-up.','Three books instead of lunch; Your bag was very well fed; books unable to share.','Make Luli’s lapse vivid and let others tease her. She should have a dry comeback; no closing assignment to check her lunch.'),
('CASE15','Mimi wants useful labels; Alio wants impressive satellite gear.','A theme tune, indoors/charging/arrival comparison and drawing a satellite all extend an already complete cardboard defeat.','Ruthless. You’ve beaten me with a piece of cardboard; adult practical win without humiliating child.','Keep direct contest between ambitious equipment and readable tag. Alio’s graciously dramatic comeback is the laugh, not a request for adult permission.'),
('CASE16','Alio sees Bibi’s hat as architecture; Bibi proudly defends her younger self.','Mimi flatly repeats the dating objective and says hat cannot date photo. Rent/extra-room thread adds length after roof-space already worked.','Excellent detective underneath it; admire respectfully / controlled limits; adult pride resisting family teasing.','Let Grandma defend her taste with authority and wit. Date-evidence phrasing can stay brief if visually obvious; avoid turning the scene into everyone mocking her age.'),
('CASE17','Alio wants the same helmet recognized as specialist railway equipment.','Professional development, promoted reader, travel points, snacks and separate seat all elaborate one accessory having a job. Bibi’s can’t-read barb risks targeting Alio by proxy.','Same helmet / changed departments; helmet buying its own ticket.','Let Alio get his proud comeback. Bibi may join the absurd world rather than repeatedly assign helmet/owner homework. Travel-points reference can go if it needs explaining.'),
('CASE18','Dilo’s watch is wrong and he dislikes admitting it.','Correcting the record before anyone made him invites a good-behavior appraisal; Luli’s same-message-to-owner reassuring tag makes the watch joke sentimental.','Watch accepts error with dignity / And its owner / Less gracefully; Luli checks times alongside him.','Maintain Dilo’s funny wounded pride and competence in fixing the record. Warmth is the shared checking action, not a speech that he has not lost his job.'),
('CASE19','Dilo likes a digital ghost but wants to test the scanner; Nini would host it.','Luli praises him for keeping fantasy out of evidence, repeating the character-growth lesson. Modern/no bedsheet and unfinished business reference can obscure the immediate library joke.','Ghost waiting outside; Nini offering book; Dilo refusing Wi-Fi password.','Make the ghost a guest with library inconveniences. Dilo should make his scanner decision without being applauded for it; prefer concrete book/password humor to metaphysics.'),
('CASE20','Nini sees a worried pear in paint; Dilo questions it; Mimi needs panel.','Mimi corrects their pretending twice and excludes it from the witness list. A six-line visual joke becomes a lecture about inanimate paint.','Very worried pear; Does it have an alibi / The pear is paint / Strong alibi.','Let Mimi need the actual panel while accepting their game. Trust the child knows what a pear-shaped smear is; stop immediately on Strong alibi.'),
('CASE21','The note has torn; Dilo wants to help without damaging it again; others need his care.','Seven expanded speeches describe good process, fairness and memory limits. Everyone becomes a reflective mini-mentor during an intimate quiet moment.','No laughing at damage; Luli asking him to check joins with her; Bibi’s Maybe/archive answer; Dilo offering exact useful care.','Protect the hush. Give Dilo a real job with a small practical invitation; no joke needed, no I-can-help-without-hurrying-paper self-explanation, no permanent sinner arc.'),
('CASE22','Alio imagines identical cases undercover; Luli spots their labels; Nini wants them home.','Witness protection may be unfamiliar at eight; cover identities, marker-pen operation, new careers and teacher explanation keep amplifying one bureaucratic conceit.','Labels ruining disguise; Nini treating cases as tired after rehearsal; Dilo unwilling to read bedtime story.','Use one instantly readable hiding-identity move. Let each reply change the situation; Nini’s play can redirect without please-don’t adult policing.'),
('CASE23','Dilo feels personally challenged by an idle scoreboard and hates leaving it.','Opening explains number envy before Mimi can puncture it; Luli embeds the whole witness task in her question; final score/witness add-on repeats rivalry.','It displayed a number / In a tone is an excellent recognizable sibling/family exchange.','Protect the three-beat argument intact and quick. Let Dilo reluctantly leave a rival for the case; avoid motivational praise.'),
('CASE24','Alio has paused his tunnel theory to inspect actual mud; Luli pauses too.','A long self-aware statement about trying this new thing converts observation into a lesson. Luli’s wanting to hear what you notice is scripted validation rather than sibling speech.','Voluntarily; what mud has to say; Mimi photographing rare quiet; Alio insisting Mom’s phone belongs in fair album.','Keep reciprocal teasing and the fair-album comeback. The story already shows Alio lowering his pointing hand: do not narrate his moral improvement again.'),
('CASE25','Parcel has been over-helped; Dilo wants nobody to touch it; Alio wants biscuits.','Mimi issues routing instructions twice; Alio explains biscuits are for people and he understands parcels, removing possible comic ambiguity.','No unauthorized helping; morale biscuits; parcel already helped too much.','Let biscuit offer need no defense. Mom can include the reader through sharing food without a final instruction about advice/handoff.'),
('THREAD120','Dilo likes his impressive solved-case stack; Mimi needs her elbow and table back.','Both things can be true sounds therapeutic; Luli’s ruler supplies a new joke before Bibi can defend his harmless vanity. Last line extends paperweight to filing Mom.','Dilo keeping stack because impressive; Bibi Let him have both; Mimi’s elbow as paperweight.','Let Dilo have earned pride plus a silly motive. Bibi is a fellow family member defending him, not validating a principle. End on a clear physical table problem.'),
('CASE26','Nini notices the absent people; Luli enjoys a witness who stays quiet; Mimi retaliates.','Nobody not raising a hand and medal/contributed nothing prolong wordplay before Luli’s favorite witness. Bibi adds investigation instructions after a potentially sweet family tag.','Nobody as witness; Luli teased for dinner-long footnote; Bibi enjoying that footnote.','Absence can be playful without making solution unclear. Keep adult and older sibling fallibility; a concise footnote counter-jab gives Luli fair return for brothers joke.'),
('CASE27','Bibi wants fragile plans safe; Alio wants to point; Dilo protests one-finger privilege.','Bibi gives care rules in all three turns, calls excuses old, warns about prodding rooms and repeats hover/sleeve distinction. She becomes a gatekeeper rather than beloved archive expert.','No heroic folding; heroic point; solving parcel to earn permission for one finger; worthy investment.','Give one crisp care rule then play the tiny heroic-point game. Bibi can win with pleasure. Do not imply children cannot touch anything or use recovered tools incorrectly.'),
('CASE28','Alio’s beautifully presented theory has no proof; Mom and Grandma admit their own versions.','Heading/straight border/crest repeat the decoration; adult admissions grow into confessions and explicit approval of Luli’s question. Decorative confidence may be abstract without physical empty card.','Decorative confidence; Mimi and Bibi asking for cards; experience as Grandma’s own flimsy cover.','Keep adult self-implication: this prevents lecture hierarchy. An empty evidence area makes joke concrete; stop on Bibi’s experience turn rather than explain the rule lesson.'),
('CASE29','Reader faces largest map; family makes room and waits together.','V9 adds a long elbow anecdote and over-specifies staring at corners. Reassurance is at risk of accumulating into coached performance, though essential shared patience is intact.','I can be quiet for one map / written in pencil; team physically making space; We’re not going anywhere.','Retain the quiet shared patience and one small sibling joke. No instruction after the reassurance; reader’s pace stays their own, without large victory or competence speeches.'),
('CASE30','Reader gets final turn; Dilo and Nini are desperate to celebrate before door opens.','Mimi repeats final-check instructions; Dilo explains noise escape; Luli’s rest-of-us-can’t-hear can sound irritated rather than precise; Nini explains why reader hears first; Bibi recaps journey.','Victory noise ownership; Luli’s concise timing limit; Nini secretly noisy too; family right behind reader.','End with held breath, anticipation and this family waiting. A short warm invitation earns belonging better than recap or praise. Do not make the door open prematurely.'),
]

findings=[]
for id,want,defect,keeper,direction in rows:
    findings.append(dict(id=id,audience='8–12 editorial inference; not child testing',comic_want_or_stake=want,current_v9_defect=defect,strong_keeper=keeper,fix_direction=direction,status='REVISE' if id not in ['CASE21','CASE29'] else 'PROTECT_AND_TRIM'))
assert len(findings)==34
out=root/'reviews/audience-diagnostic'
(out/'findings.json').write_text(json.dumps({'scope':'All 34 V9 communication scenes; family-ear and audience editorial review','basis':['diagnostic/CASE_CONTEXT_PACKET.md','diagnostic/VERSION_REFERENCE.md','diagnostic/source-scenes.json','baseline/reader-v9.md (character bios and locked story context)'],'limits':'Editorial assessment of likely reader comprehension and voice; no claim of professional psychological assessment or testing with children. Candidate review pending.','findings':findings},indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
header='''# Audience / family-ear diagnostic — rejected V9

All 34 scenes reviewed against their actual case setup and earlier wording. This is an editorial assessment for ages 8–12, not a child test or a psychological assessment. No replacement candidate was written here.

## Overall direction

V9 often gives a good joke, explains it, then returns the family to correct detective behavior. That turns affection into supervision and slows the book. The problem is not simply word count: a longer exchange can work when the next speaker wants something and changes the comic situation. A short instruction can still flatten a scene.

Keep the family’s unevenness. Mimi loses her phone and can be caught. Luli is sharp and can be caught reading instead of eating. Dilo wants to win but is also useful. Alio deserves both pointed teasing and an ally who joins his invention. Nini names things and understands people; she should not become everyone’s tiny teacher. Bibi has pride, taste and fallible memory; she need not regulate each sentence.

Best belonging signals are shared food, a defended drawing, clearing table space, someone remembering your habits, and being invited to do a useful part. They do not need to be followed by an explanation of inclusion. Maintain the unusually quiet care in 21 and collective patience in 29. The entire book need not sound equally funny at all times.

Vocabulary is not an automatic veto. A young reader can infer a harder phrase when a physical joke makes it clear. Avoid a chain of adult-office metaphors (promotion, appointment, qualifications, policy, identities) that makes following the joke harder than the case. No forced slang, no compulsory moral, no requirement that every tease apologize for itself.

## Scene findings
'''
parts=[header]
for f in findings:
    parts += [f"### {f['id']}\n",f"**Want / comic stake:** {f['comic_want_or_stake']}\n",f"**Current V9 defect:** {f['current_v9_defect']}\n",f"**Strong keeper:** {f['strong_keeper']}\n",f"**Direction:** {f['fix_direction']}\n"]
(out/'FINDINGS.md').write_text('\n'.join(parts)+'\n')
print('Wrote',out/'FINDINGS.md', 'and findings.json; covered', len(findings), 'scenes')
